These are the lines of Godot's source that this chapter followed.

They are the reflection's source, the blend, and the BRDF.

## The frame again {#c8 number=8 target=80 summary="P followed back through every stage, and three takeaways." sources="process-ssr, copy-last-frame"}

### P, from the pre-pass to the floor {#c8-walk kind=2d graph=frame focus="PRE, SSR, OPAQUE, HISTORY"}

${cue "key" {' {callout "process-ssr"}}}
Here is the path of P, the floor pixel in front of the teapot, through the frame once more.

### The depth pre-pass {#c8-walk-pre kind=2d graph=frame focus="PRE"}

P's depth and normal came from the depth pre-pass.

### The march {#c8-walk-march kind=2d graph=frame focus="ssrHiz, ssrTrace"}

Its ray was marched through the depth pyramid.

### Last frame's colour {#c8-walk-history kind=2d graph=frame focus="HISTORY, ssrTrace"}

${cue "key" {' {callout "copy-last-frame"}}} Its colour came from last frame's image.

### The blur {#c8-walk-blur kind=2d graph=frame focus="ssrFilter, ssrResolve"}

Its blur came from the floor's roughness.

### Into the floor {#c8-walk-opaque kind=2d graph=frame focus="OPAQUE"}

How much of that colour the floor shows came from P's validity.

### Three takeaways {#c8-takeaways kind=3d}

${cue "key" {opening demoRoom panelHidden {append baseRoom lowCamera}}}
${cue "key" {'
    {motion {' {cameraPath {' {pose 18.0 10.0 5.6} {pose 30.0 12.0 5.0} {pose 22.0 10.0 5.4}}}}}}}

${cue "key" {' {glide cameraDistance 5.0 sentence}}}SSR traces one ray per half-size pixel, through a pyramid of depths.

It reuses last frame's colour, so reflections of reflections build up, one bounce a frame.

${overText
    {' {floorRoughnessRange 0.15 0.3}}
    "And it blurs by roughness with a chain of mip levels, not with a blur per pixel"}.

${cue "key" {' {glide cameraYaw 24.0 sentence}}}But SSR knows only depths, normals, and last frame's colour.

${cue "key" {' {glide cameraYaw 20.0 sentence}}}So it can reflect only what was on screen.

${cue "key" {' {glide cameraDistance 5.6 sentence}}}${overText
    {' {ssrEnabledRange 1.0 0.0}}
    "What is off screen is lost"}.

What has moved lags a frame.

${over
    {' {ssrEnabledRange 0.0 1.0}}
    {overText
        {' {floorRoughnessRange 0.3 0.04}}
        f"{And the fades keep every pixel's validity at ${spoken {fadePeak}} hundredths or less, so SSR only ever covers part of the sky's reflection}"}}.

So SSR reflects only what the frame can see, and only part of what the sky would show.

### Where to read {#c8-sources kind=2d sources="process-ssr, copy-last-frame"}

These are the lines of Godot's source that this chapter returned to.

They are the passes, and the copy of last frame's image that links one frame to the next.
